{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Then he approached him… Let your servant now speak a word.</b> Since you said <b>Far be it from me to do this</b> — that you would not wish harm to come about through you, even to the guilty." "<b>Let your servant speak.</b> In order to inform you of the harm that would come about through you if you do this." "<b>And let your anger not burn.</b> When I say to you that you have brought this harm upon us against our will." "<b>For you are like Pharaoh.</b> For my speaking words against you is not because I disregard you, for indeed you are regarded in my eyes like Pharaoh, who is the king."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:34:31.878237831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}